 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Keep it simple. Welcomes, toasts, and short speech or two. Lots of laughter. You can ask someone who knows the couple well to share a few minutes about their love story. Or ask each of their closest friends to give a small, heartfelt speech. A short ritual can work. A candle, a simple blessing, or a few moments of silence can feel special and meaningful. Just make sure it' not the main focus of the ceremony. Planting a tree is a lovely touch. Make sure it' something the couple can see from wherever they' living, and give it good edging protect it from the lawnmower. I' glad. Keep it simple, and let the couple have few moments alone without everyone talking.",
